WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.450
At some point in their careers, these celebs
looked at their artistic and professional

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.760
achievements, fame, fortune, and shelves full
of awards and said, "This isn't for me."

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.140
Then they left acting behind and were fortunate
enough to discover the things they really

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.140
wanted to do.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.600
After five seasons of the popular Comedy Central
sketch show Key &amp; Peele, it was obvious that

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.740
Jordan Peele would move on to something even
bigger.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.460
Most people would have predicted starring
roles in a string of big-screen comedies.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.460
He threw the world for a loop when he chose
to be a filmmaker instead, writing and directing

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.370
the satirical horror movie Get Out, for which
he won the Academy Award for Best Original

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:36.980
Screenplay.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.920
In other words, this new trajectory suits
Peele.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.920
One of the best-reviewed movies of 2017, Get
Out clinched his decision, but so did one

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.630
of the worst-reviewed movies, according to
Complex.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.280
During his acceptance speech for best rookie
director at the Directors Guild of America

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.079
Awards in February 2018, Peele said,

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:56.680
"The Emoji Movie actually helped me quit acting.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.540
I was offered the role of Poop.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.580
This is true.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.220
I would not make this up."

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.100
"What?!"

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.340
There was a brief period after the release
of The Blair Witch Project in 1999 in which

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.440
many people thought that Heather Donahue would
never work again because she was actually

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:12.940
dead.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.460
That's how effective Blair Witch was as the
pioneering classic of modern "found footage"-style

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.480
horror movies.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.900
When the world realized the movie was fiction,
Donahue got very famous very fast, but was

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:29.400
also so closely tied to the film that she
couldn't keep a decent career going, according

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.400
to People magazine.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.920
"I wasn't getting to do things that I was
very proud of putting out into the world."

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.220
And so she gave it all up…for marijuana.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:43.580
In her 2012 memoir GrowGirl: How My Life After
The Blair Witch Project Went to Pot, Donahue

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.869
recounted how she followed a boyfriend into
the world of high-scale marijuana farming

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:48.860
in California.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:55.360
The central cast of the raunchy 2002 cult
classic The Sweetest Thing Cameron Diaz, Selma

00:01:55.370 --> 00:02:00.070
Blair, and Christina Applegate reunited in
2018 for an Entertainment Weekly profile.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.130
When asked if the actresses ever hung out,
Diaz said she'd like to and that she had the

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.659
time, off-handedly noting that she's currently,
quote, "literally doing nothing," then adding

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:11.749
that she's "actually retired."

00:02:11.749 --> 00:02:15.919
A few weeks earlier, Blair claimed to Metro
that since appearing in the remake of Annie

00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:21.680
in 2014 and marrying Good Charlotte guitarist
Benji Madden in 2015, Diaz had quietly quit

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.220
Hollywood.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.460
She explained,

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.720
"Cameron's retired from acting.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.340
I mean, she doesn't need to make any more
films, she has a pretty great life, I don't

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.129
know what it would take to bring her back.

00:02:30.129 --> 00:02:30.920
She's happy."

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.779
You might remember Lisa Jakub from such unforgettable
mid-1990s blockbusters as Mrs. Doubtfire and

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.720
Independence Day.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.440
But around the year 2000, she quit acting.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.319
In 2013, Jakub wrote on her blog,

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:48.209
"The competition and the politics and the
superficial nature of the industry started

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:48.700
to get to me.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.800
I felt like a phony who was trying to live
someone else's dream."

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.080
She added that the nastiness of Hollywood
increased her anxiety and depression, so she

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.189
left show business before she could turn into,
quote, "a train wreck of a former child actor."

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:06.190
These days, Jakub plays a lot of roles, just
offscreen: in addition to her blog, she's

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:10.900
published books, she's a public speaker, and
she teaches yoga and writing.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:16.639
Ariana Richards was a very successful child
and teen star in the late 1980s and early

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:22.540
1990s, appearing in movies like Prancer, Tremors,
and, most famously, Jurassic Park.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.820
Richards appeared in a few more films after
the release of that box office smash in 1993,

00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:32.180
but she's basically retired from the art of
filmmaking in favor of the art of painting.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.760
Oddly, it was Jurassic Park that inspired
her career shift and artistic awakening.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.200
Richards told People magazine in 2011,

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.959
"I wanted to boil down the whole experience
of Jurassic into my art.

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:44.079
I painted an image of me from the Jell-O scene.

00:03:44.079 --> 00:03:48.339
I ended up presenting Steven [Spielberg] with
one of my paintings at the end of filming."

00:03:48.339 --> 00:03:54.540
"My last painting of a dinosaur was the self
portrait I did as Lex with the superimposed

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.840
image of the raptor kind of going across my
face."

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.960
Nowadays, Richards has her own art gallery
in Salem, Oregon, called Gallery Ariana.

